<ContentPage
  title="When to book for the Four Days Marches — Vierdaagse Logeren"
  description="When should you book accommodation for the Four Days Marches? Practical tips from Vierdaagse Logeren so you don't end up without a place to stay."
  locale="en"
  h1="Book your Four Days Marches stay in time"
>
  <p>
    The same story every year: in June people think "it'll be fine" and end up empty-
    handed in July. The Four Days Marches brings thousands of walkers and visitors to
    Nijmegen and the surrounding area, and the number of places to stay doesn't grow
    with demand. Book early and you'll have plenty of choice at a normal price. Wait,
    and you'll pay more for less — or have to look further afield.
  </p>

  <h2>The rule of thumb: earlier is better</h2>
  <p>
    There's no hard deadline, but there is a clear pattern: campsites and centrally
    located accommodations are typically the first to sell out, often months before the
    event. Wait until a few weeks before, and you'll mostly be looking at options
    outside Nijmegen itself.
  </p>
  <p class="callout">
    Rule of thumb: start looking as soon as next year's dates are announced — that's
    usually well before summer.
  </p>

  <h2>Who should book first</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>International visitors</strong> — arranging travel time, flights, and
      leave already forces early planning. Combine that with your accommodation search.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Groups</strong> — the bigger the group, the earlier you need to be. A
      spot for 2 is easier to find last-minute than one for 8.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Anyone wanting a specific location</strong> — close to the start/finish,
      or specific facilities — has the least flexibility and therefore the most
      urgency.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What happens if you're too late</h2>
  <p>No need to panic — there are always options, they just shift:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Further from Nijmegen (Wijchen, Groesbeek, Cuijk, and other surrounding towns)</li>
    <li>More expensive, as scarcity drives up the price</li>
    <li>Less choice in type of stay — camping typically fills up before hotel rooms further away</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Quick checklist</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Note the Four Days Marches dates as soon as they're announced</li>
    <li>Plan your travel time and transport</li>
    <li>
      Choose your type of stay — see <a href="/en/camping">camping</a>,
      <a href="/en/particuliere-verhuur">private stays</a>, or
      <a href="/en/hotels-bb">hotels &amp; B&amp;Bs</a>
    </li>
    <li>Book as soon as something fits, even if it feels "early"</li>
  </ol>
</ContentPage>
